that you need to be in the Aura to <u>use</u> the Charm. I believe there would be a statement elsewhere clarifying that this means that ending an Aura takes the Charm down with it, I shall endeavour to find it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T13:45:23-08:00","id":1292848,"title":"","content":"There could be scene-long Charms which would lose their Aura effects if you lose the Aura, but only if they have explicitly graduated effects. If the Charm just requires you to have an Aura to invoke the Charm, it shouldn't be affected by losing the Aura unless it has a duration of &quot;Aura&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T15:01:54-08:00","id":1292863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292848#post1292848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could be scene-long Charms which would lose their Aura effects if you lose the Aura, but only if they have explicitly graduated effects. If the Charm just requires you to have an Aura to invoke the Charm, it shouldn't be affected by losing the Aura unless it has a duration of &quot;Aura&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s my interpretation as well but I can\u2019t find it spelled out explicitly and I\u2019m basically just going of implications from the writing.<br /> <br /> I know when I write mechanics I tend to over explain things to my own detriment but sometimes I wish wordcount wasn\u2019t an issue:/<br /> <br /> Somewhat relatedly, do Charms with the Perilous keyword deactivate while crashed? Or can they simply not be activated. I\u2019ve always assumed they ended but it\u2019s not actually stated anyplace I can find","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 02-28-2019, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T17:51:57-08:00","id":1292891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292863#post1292863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s my interpretation as well but I can\u2019t find it spelled out explicitly and I\u2019m basically just going of implications from the writing.<br /> <br /> I know when I write mechanics I tend to over explain things to my own detriment but sometimes I wish wordcount wasn\u2019t an issue:/<br /> <br /> Somewhat relatedly, do Charms with the Perilous keyword deactivate while crashed? Or can they simply not be activated. I\u2019ve always assumed they ended but it\u2019s not actually stated anyplace I can find</div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel like in the spirit of the charm they must deactivate, although I haven\u2019t seen any definitive I\u2019ve reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T19:39:05-08:00","id":1292909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292891#post1292891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel like in the spirit of the charm they must deactivate, although I haven\u2019t seen any definitive I\u2019ve reply.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were true, there wouldn't be a point to having &quot;Aura&quot; durations.<br /> <br /> The common ground between Aura of Grasping Branches and Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit is that they both require you to have the right Aura to use at all. The difference is that only Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit ends when you lose that Aura. Grasping Branches continues to work fine because it has a scene-length duration and doesn't specify that it loses any power when you lose the Wood Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T19:43:21-08:00","id":1292911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292909#post1292909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were true, there wouldn't be a point to having &amp;quot;Aura&amp;quot; durations.<br /> <br /> The common ground between Aura of Grasping Branches and Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit is that they both require you to have the right Aura to use at all. The difference is that only Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit ends when you lose that Aura. Grasping Branches continues to work fine because it has a scene-length duration and doesn't specify that it loses any power when you lose the Wood Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Body of Deadly Thorns is a better example as aura of grasping branches lacks the Aura keyword","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T19:52:26-08:00","id":1292913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292911#post1292911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Body of Deadly Thorns is a better example as aura of grasping branches lacks the Aura keyword</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, got the two mixed up.<br /> <br /> My point still stands. We don't want to lose levels of detail like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Level 1: Requires no Aura to invoke, is not empowered by Aura<br /> <br /> Level 2: Requires no Aura to invoke, is empowered by Aura<br /> <br /> Level 3: Requires Aura to invoke, because you need to spend the Aura<br /> <br /> Level 4: Requires Aura to invoke, ends without Aura<br /> <br /> Level 5: Requires Aura to invoke, but merely loses power without Aura<br /> <br /> Level 6: Requires Aura to invoke, but loses no power without Aura","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:15:45-08:00","id":1292922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292830-an-aura-question?p=1292909#post1292909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were true, there wouldn't be a point to having &quot;Aura&quot; durations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, when I started looking back over the rules, that discrepancy in my assumptions stood out to me in a way that it had not before.<br /> <br /> I'm actually interested to look back over the Charms, and see if a few Aura keyword scene-long Charms come across differently with this clarification in mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:22:41-08:00","id":1292924,"title":"","content":"Answered in ask the devs:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1292919#post1292919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, unless it has &amp;quot;Duration: Aura.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No, unless it specifically says so.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:32:21-08:00","id":1292926,"title":"","content":"Actually, let me reverse levels 3-6.<br /> <br /> <br /> Level 1: Requires no Aura to invoke, is not empowered by Aura<br /> <br /> Level 2: Requires no Aura to invoke, is empowered by Aura<br /> <br /> Level 3: Requires Aura to invoke, but loses no power without Aura<br /> <br /> Level 4: Requires Aura to invoke, but loses some power without Aura<br /> <br /> Level 5: Requires Aura to invoke, ends completely without Aura<br /> <br /> Level 6: Requires Aura to invoke, because you need to spend the Aura","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}